laurel 3080: LAUREL SWAP: the VM compressor runs with a swap file, as on a real iPhone. [V code] Both Mi A3 kernels (SWEET: CONFIG_JETSAM, no CONFIG_FREEZE) start the compressor without swap, so a full compressor kills the largest compressed process (mediaserverd at 2.6 GB in the 11-04 logs). New osfmk/vm/laurel_swap.c + laurel_swap_core.h (pure decision, host test scripts/laurel/test-swap.sh): before vm_config_init reads vm_compressor_mode, NO_SWAP/NOT_CONFIGURED -> COMPRESSOR_WITH_SWAP (a freezer kernel: FREEZER_WITH_SWAP) unless a vm_compressor= boot-arg was given; the kernel then writes full compressed segments to /private/var/vm/swapfileN (encrypted, 128 MiB each, at most 5 = 640 MiB, made on demand). Self-check: the first swap file made, or the first failure to make one (read-only root, no directory, no space: the kernel then runs compressor-only as before), is reported once; one line a minute with free/active/inactive/speculative/wired, compressor pages and bytes, segments, swap used, memorystatus level. Kill switch laurelswap=0. The xnu-8796 hook is in vm_fault.c (vm_fault_init parses vm_compressor=); on xnu-12377 the mode is a TUNABLE_DT read in vm_pageout.c vm_config_init: rule drop_file + post/9024. docs/laurel_sprout/memory.md.

